Ladybird sets a video decoder’s max_pixels through av_opt_set_int(),
which finds the field through the library’s own option table, since its
decoders run against libavcodec majors whose AVCodecContext layouts
differ. Gecko’s FFmpegDataDecoder sets the same kind of limit by writing
max_pixels directly, which is safe there: Gecko compiles that code once
per libavcodec major, against that major’s own headers. Blink sets no
max_pixels at all, and WebKit leaves decoding to GStreamer. (All from
reading the engines’ source.)
